WEBVTT

1 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Okay, let's get started. This session is about the Manage Devices prototype. I want to agree the two device types, the Add Devices wizard, asset tag validation, retiring devices, and what we do with the approval workflow.

2 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Let's start with the two device types. We have IT-managed and Faculty-registered. Kofi, can you recap where each one comes from?

3 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:00:35.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Sure. Both types live in Asset Registry, which is the system of record for devices. IT-managed devices also have a counterpart in the Room Booking Manager, and that is where the faculty, floor and room assignment is kept. They are born READY.

4 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
And the Faculty-registered ones? Who creates those?

5 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:40.000
An AV technician or a faculty team registers them, either through Atrium or on a Building Controller. Either way they end up in Asset Registry first. Then the Building Controller completes the record with Faculty, Floor, Room and Device IP. We call that the complement.

6 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Right, and every building has its own controller. A campus can have several, each with its own database, so Atrium has to ask all of them for the complement.

7 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:10.000
So what does the table show before the controller has reported anything?

8 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Dashes. If a device has not been assigned to a controller, the five columns just show a dash. If the controller is assigned but only partly reported, only the missing fields show a dash.

9 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:50.000
And if the controller is unreachable, those five columns collapse into one cell with a warning icon that says information cannot be read from Building Controller and then its hostname.

10 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:05.000
Do we still need a Type column, then?

11 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:20.000
No. The toggle in the navbar is the type indicator, so the Type column is gone. IT-managed is the default when the page loads.

12 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:35.000
And the scope picker is Campus only for both modes. We removed the Building Controller selector.

13 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:50.000
That is fine by me. Anything about individual controllers belongs in Manage Infrastructure, not on the device page.

14 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:03:50.000 --> 00:04:05.000
One more thing for the Faculty-registered view. There is an info banner above the table that says devices shown are faculty-registered room devices.

15 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:20.000
That works. Can we move on to the wizard?

16 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:35.000
Yes. Add Devices is a two-step wizard. Step one is Provide asset tags, step two is Review and register Devices. The type is locked to whatever the toggle is set to.

17 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:50.000
Why lock it? I would have expected a type picker.

18 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:04:50.000 --> 00:05:10.000
We had one for a while, but the page is already in a single mode, so the picker added nothing. Instead the footer shows a note: devices added to this Campus will have the Managed type, or the Registered type.

19 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:25.000
The title only shows the campus. Add Devices to, then the campus name.

20 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:40.000
And how do people enter the tags?

21 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:05:40.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Either upload a file or add them manually. The upload tab inherits the campus from the page. The manual tab has a Campus picker and a text area. The upload is mocked in the prototype, it just loads a sample file.

22 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:15.000
For validation, an asset tag must be 8 to 14 letters or digits. Commas, semicolons, spaces and line breaks are accepted as separators.

23 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:30.000
Our real tags look like PRJNORT1001. Three letters for the device kind, then the campus code, then a number. Projector, microphone, door reader, room panel.

24 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:45.000
Should the wizard enforce that prefix?

25 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:06:45.000 --> 00:07:00.000
Not in this phase. We only check length and characters. A prefix check could come later once the naming convention is final.

26 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:15.000
Format problems show inline in step two, with the message: Invalid asset tag, use 8 to 14 alphanumeric characters. There is also a show errors only switch and a search box.

27 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:30.000
Duplicates are different. We check them when you click Add Devices, against Asset Registry, under both types.

28 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:45.000
Why not show those inline as well?

29 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:07:45.000 --> 00:08:05.000
Because it needs a registry lookup per tag. So a conflict comes as a red toast: Atrium couldn't register the devices, selected devices already in use on that type's Asset Registry. One toast per type that had conflicts.

30 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:20.000
When that toast fires, the wizard stays open and the rows that were added are removed from the list, so only the problem tags remain.

31 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:35.000
And on success you get a green toast, something like 3 Devices added to NORT on Managed.

32 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:50.000
What if someone closes the wizard halfway through typing?

33 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:08:50.000 --> 00:09:05.000
If there is pending input, a small confirm popover opens with two buttons, Keep editing and Discard. A successful commit skips it.

34 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:20.000
Next, retiring devices. Which statuses can be retired?

35 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:35.000
Pending approval, Ready and Provisioned. Active devices cannot be retired, because their certificates have already been issued.

36 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:50.000
Yes, Active devices need to be decommissioned outside Atrium first. Moving from Ready to Provisioned to Active also happens outside Atrium, it is not a button in this tool.

37 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:09:50.000 --> 00:10:05.000
The Retire button is red, hidden until a campus is chosen, and disabled until you select rows that are eligible. It works for both device types.

38 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:20.000
Now the approval workflow. Faculty Coordinators used to approve every Faculty-registered device, and honestly nobody wanted that step.

39 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:35.000
Agreed, so we are deprecating it. Approve and Reject stay in the code but the buttons are hidden in every mode.

40 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:50.000
That also means new devices are born READY for both types, so nothing new lands in Pending approval. The status stays in the lifecycle for old records only.

41 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:10:50.000 --> 00:11:05.000
And the Faculty-registered sample data reflects that: only Active, Ready and Retired.

42 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:20.000
Does Updated by come from the new history feature?

43 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:40.000
No. Updated by and Updated at come straight from the Asset Registry device record. The history feature is on demand only, a Show history command later, and we do not fetch it when listing devices.

44 "Ravi Iyer" (1063)
00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:55.000
Also worth saying, there is no sync from Asset Registry to the controllers today. A device can exist in the registry before any controller knows it.

45 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:11:55.000 --> 00:12:10.000
That is fine. Pre-registering a device before it reaches a room is a normal scenario for us.

46 "Kofi Mensah" (1057)
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:25.000
Open question for the backend: when we fan out and one controller is unreachable, do we return partial results with a warning, or fail the whole request?

47 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:40.000
Let's note that as a decision for the Atrium server team. And whether Faculty-registered devices ever reach Provisioned, we need the registry team to confirm.

48 "Hannah Lindqvist" (1071)
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:55.000
Should the wizard warn when a tag is not on any controller yet?

49 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:12:55.000 --> 00:13:10.000
Good question, that is a UX call. I will add it to the open list.

50 "Ines Moreau" (1042)
00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:30.000
Summary: two types with campus-only scope, a locked-type wizard with format checks inline and duplicate checks at commit, retire from three statuses, and approval deprecated. Thanks everyone.
